<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="roast-gar-butt" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Roasted Garlic Butternut Soup</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>1 whole garlic bulb</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon olive oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 medium butternut squash (3 lb), peeled and cubed</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 large onion, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 tablespoons butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>3 \frac{1}{4}</m> cups water</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cups broth</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon paprika</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>9 tablespoons crumbled blue cheese</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Remove papery outer skin from garlic (do not peel or separate cloves).  Cut top off of garlic bulb.  Brush with oil; wrap in heavy-duty foil.  Bake at <m>425^\circ</m> for 30 to 35 minutes or until softened.  Cool for 10 to 15 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Meanwhile, in a Dutch oven, saute the squash, sweet potato and onion in butter until crisp-tender.  Add the water, broth, paprika, pepper and salt; squeeze softened garlic into pan.  Bring to a boil.  Reduce heat; cover and simmer for 20 to 25 minutes or until vegetables are tender.  Cool slightly.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a food processor, process soup in batches until smooth.  Return all to pan and heat through.  Ladle into bowls; top with blue cheese.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>